{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790970230,"nonce":"L6GfslbcTBUOq4cqqbzGOkpNKUE=","title":"An @:op defined on the right operand's type is not applied unless @:commutative","message":"Row: Issue8427.\n\ntast_to_hir.rs' binary `@:op` rewrite looks up the operator on the LHS type, and on the RHS type\nonly for `@:commutative` methods. For `Int + A`, Haxe applies A's `@:op(a+b) f(a:A, b:A)` with\noperands in source order, since Int converts via `from Int`. `x += (10:A)` skips the op too.","files":null}]}